\par\par \b \uc2 DJ 3rd UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Advisers Urge  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  To Stabilize Rupee\b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2011\par 12:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- Top advisers to prime minister say using \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to curb rupee fall an option\par \par \uc2 -- Finance ministry official says no plans for capital controls\par \par \uc2 -- Finance minister says capital outflow a matter of concern\par \par \uc2 (Updates \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level in 4th paragraph)\par \par \uc2 By Prasanta Sahu and Sudeep Jain\par \par \uc2 Of Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stabilize the rupee, two senior advisers to the prime minister said Wednesday, as the local unit tumbled to a fresh record low against the U.S. dollar for a third straight session.\par \par \uc2 The comments from C. Rangarajan, chairman of the Prime Minister's Economic Advisory Council, and panel member M. Govinda Rao come as the rupee continues its free fall because of global risk aversion due to the euro-zone crisis and worries over India's high inflation and slowing economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The recent slump of the rupee, Asia's worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, has increased calls for strong action from authorities, but the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has maintained that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets only to manage volatility.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was quoted at INR53.70 late Wednesday in Asia, after trading as high as INR53.88, compared with its previous peak of INR53.515, reached Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Rangarajan blamed the rupee's recent weakness on the temporary mismatch between capital inflows and a yawning current-account gap.\par \par \uc2 "The policy options are, if it is temporary, then the [\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] reserves are there, which can be used by the RBI at an appropriate time," he said on the sidelines of a conference.\par \par \uc2 India's current-account gap is expected to exceed 3% of gross domestic product this fiscal year through March, from 2.6% last year as tepid global demand dims export prospects.\par \par \uc2 Asia's third-largest economy has traditionally relied on healthy capital inflows to fund the current-account deficit, but persistent euro-zone worries have prompted investors to flee emerging economies such as India, reducing overseas inflows to a trickle.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Wednesday, a senior finance ministry official said India has no plan to curb any capital outflow to help arrest the rupee's slide. The official declined to be named.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee, however, admitted Wednesday that capital outflows are a matter of concern.\par \par \uc2 RBI Deputy Governor Subir Gokarn recently said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use all possible measures, including strategic capital controls, if the risk of the rupee depreciating escalates.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Investors Services Wednesday said India's heavy dependence on energy imports and persistently high inflation provide limited headroom for its regulated, import-dependent sectors to cope with higher import bills brought on by a weakened \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Prasanta Sahu and Sudeep Jain, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Mukesh Jagota in New Delhi contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 14, 2011 06:56 ET (11:56 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111214e7ce002qy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
