\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For December 14\b0\par\par\uc2 1,786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2011\par 08:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN CONTINUES TO SUPPORT EUROPE AT EFSF AUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan slightly increased its share of bond-buying in the latest auction by Europe's bailout fund, Japanese government officials said Wednesday, in a sign of continued support for European efforts to contain the region's debt crisis. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: JAPAN PUBLIC PENSION FUND TO STICK WITH EUROPEAN BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's public pension fund, the world's largest with assets totaling Y109 trillion, plans to hold onto its euro-denominated bond holdings, despite other domestic financial institutions backing away amid Europe's deepening sovereign debt crisis. (published 0227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA BANK REGULATOR TO DELAY IMPLEMENTING NEW STANDARDS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banking regulator has decided to postpone the implementation of new regulatory requirements for commercial banks in a bid to ensure adequate lending to support economic growth, the Economic Information Daily reported Wednesday. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDIA OFFICIAL SAYS NO PLANS FOR CAPITAL CONTROLS TO STEM RUPEE'S FALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India has no plan to curb any capital outflow to help arrest the rupee's slide, a senior finance ministry official said Wednesday, even as the local unit tumbled to a fresh record low against the U.S. dollar for the third consecutive session. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INDIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PM ADVISER: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SHOULD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NOW TO STABILIZE RUPEE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to stabilize the rupee, M. Govinda Rao, a member of the Prime Minister's Economic Advisory Council, said Wednesday. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN CONSUMER MOOD SINKS AS EUROPE FEARS RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian consumer sentiment plunged in December as rising unemployment and heightened fears linked to Europe's debt crisis swamped news of cuts in interest rates over recent months. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL: YUAN QFII TO LAUNCH IN NEAR TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing's plan to allow foreign investors to buy mainland stocks and bonds using yuan raised offshore will be launched "in the near term", a People's Bank of China official said Wednesday, without specifying the time frame. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PLEDGES TO ENSURE GROWTH, SOCIAL STABILITY IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese leaders pledged on Wednesday to maintain economic growth and social stability next year, even as economic risks are on the rise. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER: GRIP ON PROPERTY MARKET CANNOT BE LOOSENED - XINHUA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's regulation of its property market cannot be loosened, despite the progress made in cooling the sector so far, the official Xinhua News Agency cited a government researcher as saying. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA NOVEMBER WHOLESALE PRICE INDEX UP 9.11% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's inflation slowed to 9.11% in November from the previous month's provisional reading of 9.73%, according to data released by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry Wednesday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA PRIME MINISTER: AIMING FOR 9% ANNUAL GROWTH IN 5-YEAR PLAN STARTING 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's planners aim for the economy to grow at 9% annually in the 12th five-year plan period which will begin on April 1, 2012, Prime Minister Manmohan Singh said Wednesday. (published 0519 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA FINANCE MINISTER: MUST TURN ATTENTION TO REVIVING GROWTH AS QUICKLY AS POSSIBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian policymakers must now their shift focus from taming inflation to reviving economic growth, Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee said Wednesday. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WORLD BANK: CUT INDONESIA 2012 BASELINE GROWTH FORECAST TO 6.2% VS 6.3% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The World Bank Wednesday cut its baseline forecast of Indonesia's 2012 economic growth to 6.2% from 6.3%, after downgrading its growth projection for Indonesia's main trading partners to a collective 3.5% from 3.9%. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECONOMISTS IN MAS SURVEY EXPECT SINGAPORE 4Q GDP TO RISE 4.4% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists surveyed by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore expect local economic growth to slow more sharply than they had estimated three months earlier, because of a worsening global economic environment, a report showed Wednesday. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OLYMPUS FILES APR-SEP EARNINGS, MEETS DEADLINE TO AVOID DELISTING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Troubled \f28 \uc2 \f2 Olympus Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Wednesday submitted long-delayed earnings results covering the fiscal second quarter ended September, meeting a critical deadline to keep its shares listed for the immediate future. (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OLYMPUS EX-CEO WOODFORD: WOULD LIKE TO AVOID PROXY FIGHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ousted former chief executive of scandal-ridden \f28 \uc2 \f2 Olympus Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday he wants to avoid a confrontational battle with the company over the selection of a new board in the wake of a large-scale accounting scandal. (published 0543 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: NEXON STAGES TEPID DEBUT ON TOKYO BOURSE, BIGGEST IPO IN JAPAN THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Under the weight of broad market weakness, online video game company Nexon Co. received a tepid reception from the market in Japan's biggest initial public offering this year of about $1.2 billion, with its shares ending the morning session 0.5% below the premarket fixed offering price. (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: APA BIDS FOR AUSTRALIAN RIVAL TO EXPLOIT GAS DEMAND SURGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's biggest owner of gas pipelines \f28 \uc2 \f2 APA Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Wednesday made a takeover offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hastings Diversified Utilities Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  that values the target at 1.06 billion Australian dollars, as it expands its footprint ahead of an expected boom in domestic gas production. (published 0015 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HTC: US TRADE BODY RULING ON PATENT CASE VS APPLE DELAYED TO MONDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HTC Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday the U.S. International Trade Commission notified the Taiwanese smartphone maker that it had postponed its ruling on a patent case brought against the firm by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to Monday. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INOTERA TO RAISE FUNDS THROUGH PRIVATE PLACEMENT AFTER SHELVING SHARE SALE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwanese memory chip maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Inotera Memories Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it shelved its plan to sell up to 1.1 billion new shares on the open market due to poor market conditions, and that it would instead make a private placement of stock or convertible bonds to its major shareholders. (published 0221 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ZYL RECEIVES INITIAL BIDS, APPOINTS MACQUARIE UNIT TO ADVISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Africa-focused coal developer Zyl Ltd. said Wednesday it has appointed a unit of Macquarie Capital to advise on two approaches to buy or partner the company. (published 0003 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WESTPAC SAYS EUROPE WOES MAY REDUCE CREDIT AVAILABILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Westpac Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . warned Wednesday that Europe's debt woes will continue to impact the price and possibly even the availability of credit to Australia's banking sector. (published 2318 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MACQUARIE SELLS 9.9% STAKE IN KEMBLE WATER TO ABU DHABI INVESTMENT AUTHORITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macquarie Infrastructure and Real Assets, or MIRA, has sold a 9.9% stake in Kemble Water Holdings Ltd., the holding company of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thames Water\f28 \uc2 \f2 , to Infinity Investments S.A., a wholly owned subsidiary of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Abu Dhabi Investment Authority\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TELSTRA APPOINTS FORMER AXA APH CHIEF ANDREW PENN AS CFO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's biggest telecommunications company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telstra Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it has appointed former \f28 \uc2 \f2 AXA Asia Pacific Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . boss Andrew Penn as its chief financial officer and group managing director, finance, replacing \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Stanhope\f28 \uc2 \f2  who is retiring. (published 2219 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RESTAURANT BRANDS SAYS 3Q SALES DOWN SLIGHTLY ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fast-food chain operator Restaurant Brands Ltd. said Wednesday its total sales for the third quarter were down slightly on the year largely due to store closures in Christchurch following the earthquakes and the sale of Pizza Hut stores to independent franchisees. (published 2132 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NZ OIL & GAS\f28 \uc2 \f2  AGREES TO TAKE 40% STAKE IN TUNISIA CONCESSION WITH OIL FIELD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand Oil & Gas Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has agreed to take a 40% stake in a Tunisian concession that includes an oil field which could be brought into production as early as 2014, the company said in a statement. (published 0055 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHOW TAI FOOK: RETAIL TRANCHE OF IPO ABOUT 6.62 TIMES OVERSUBSCRIBED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chow Tai Fook Jewellery Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday the institutional portion of its US$2 billion Hong Kong initial public offering, accounting for 95% of the whole offer, was "moderately" oversubscribed, while the retail portion was about 6.62 times oversubscribed. (published 0126 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES COME OFF LOWS IN CHOPPY TRADE; EXPORTERS DOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets came off their lows in choppy trade Wednesday, while regional exporters underperformed amid a gloomy global growth outlook as investors found little inspiration from the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy meeting. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 COMMODITIES/ENERGY:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA MOVES TOWARD NEW A$10B QUEENSLAND COAL PORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia edged closer to the creation of a new 10 billion Australian dollar port focused on exporting coal to Asia when the state of Queensland allocated land to units of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brookfield Asset Management Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and India's Adani Group for two terminals at Dudgeon Point on Wednesday. (published 2307 GMT Tuesday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JBIC: TO LEND UP TO $600 MLN TO QATAR'S BARZAN GAS PROJECT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japan Bank For International Cooperation said Wednesday that it has signed a contract to help finance the Barzan gas project in Qatar with a loan of up to $600 million, earmarked for construction of a natural gas processing plant to be built by Japanese plant maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 JGC Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0635 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA TO DECIDE ON FOOD SECURITY LAW AFTER TALKS WITH STATES - FARM MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India will decide on a food security law that promises to give cheap food grains to 63.5% of the country's 1.2 billion population after discussions with state governments, Farm Minister Sharad Pawar said Wednesday. (published 0554 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL 2011 COFFEE EXPORTS LIKELY $23.5 BLN, UP 41% -ICO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 14-12-11 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The value of coffee exports in calendar 2011 is forecast at $23.5 billion, up about 41%, as global demand is robust, the International Coffee Organization said. (published 0358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM 2011-12 COFFEE OUTPUT LIKELY 10% HIGHER AT 20.6 MLN BAGS -USDA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's coffee production this marketing year will likely reach 20.6 million 60-kilogram bags, up about 10%, on the back of greater acreage and higher yields due to better agricultural practices, the U.S. Department of Agriculture said. (published 0326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA OCTOBER WHEAT EXPORTS FELL TO 1.2 MLN TONS, DOWN 20% ON MONTH -ABS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The volume of wheat exported from Australia fell to 1.2 million metric tons in October, down 285,000 tons, or 20%, from shipments in September and down 469,000 tons compared with last October, the Australian Bureau of Statistics reported Wednesday. (published 0050 GMT) [ 14-12-11 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111214e7ce000bq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
