\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2011\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN CONTINUES TO SUPPORT EUROPE AT EFSF AUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan slightly increased its share of bond-buying in the latest auction by Europe's bailout fund, Japanese government officials said Wednesday, in a sign of continued support for European efforts to contain the region's debt crisis. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INTERVIEW: JAPAN PUBLIC PENSION FUND TO STICK WITH EUROPEAN BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's public pension fund, the world's largest with assets totaling Y109 trillion, plans to hold onto its euro-denominated bond holdings, despite other domestic financial institutions backing away amid Europe's deepening sovereign debt crisis. (published 0227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA BANK REGULATOR TO DELAY IMPLEMENTING NEW STANDARDS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banking regulator has decided to postpone the implementation of new regulatory requirements for commercial banks in a bid to ensure adequate lending to support economic growth, the Economic Information Daily reported Wednesday. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: INDIA OFFICIAL SAYS NO PLANS FOR CAPITAL CONTROLS TO STEM RUPEE'S FALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India has no plan to curb any capital outflow to help arrest the rupee's slide, a senior finance ministry official said Wednesday, even as the local unit tumbled to a fresh record low against the U.S. dollar for the third consecutive session. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INDIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PM ADVISER: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SHOULD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NOW TO STABILIZE RUPEE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to stabilize the rupee, M. Govinda Rao, a member of the Prime Minister's Economic Advisory Council, said Wednesday. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN CONSUMER MOOD SINKS AS EUROPE FEARS RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian consumer sentiment plunged in December as rising unemployment and heightened fears linked to Europe's debt crisis swamped news of cuts in interest rates over recent months. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL: YUAN QFII TO LAUNCH IN NEAR TERM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing's plan to allow foreign investors to buy mainland stocks and bonds using yuan raised offshore will be launched "in the near term", a People's Bank of China official said Wednesday, without specifying the time frame. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA PLEDGES TO ENSURE GROWTH, SOCIAL STABILITY IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese leaders pledged on Wednesday to maintain economic growth and social stability next year, even as economic risks are on the rise. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER: GRIP ON PROPERTY MARKET CANNOT BE LOOSENED - XINHUA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's regulation of its property market cannot be loosened, despite the progress made in cooling the sector so far, the official Xinhua News Agency cited a government researcher as saying. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA NOVEMBER WHOLESALE PRICE INDEX UP 9.11% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's inflation slowed to 9.11% in November from the previous month's provisional reading of 9.73%, according to data released by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry Wednesday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA PRIME MINISTER: AIMING FOR 9% ANNUAL GROWTH IN 5-YEAR PLAN STARTING 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's planners aim for the economy to grow at 9% annually in the 12th five-year plan period which will begin on April 1, 2012, Prime Minister Manmohan Singh said Wednesday. (published 0519 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA FINANCE MINISTER: MUST TURN ATTENTION TO REVIVING GROWTH AS QUICKLY AS POSSIBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian policymakers must now their shift focus from taming inflation to reviving economic growth, Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee said Wednesday. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: WORLD BANK: CUT INDONESIA 2012 BASELINE GROWTH FORECAST TO 6.2% VS 6.3% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The World Bank Wednesday cut its baseline forecast of Indonesia's 2012 economic growth to 6.2% from 6.3%, after downgrading its growth projection for Indonesia's main trading partners to a collective 3.5% from 3.9%. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECONOMISTS IN MAS SURVEY EXPECT SINGAPORE 4Q GDP TO RISE 4.4% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists surveyed by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore expect local economic growth to slow more sharply than they had estimated three months earlier, because of a worsening global economic environment, a report showed Wednesday. (published 0400 GMT) [ 14-12-11 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111214e7ce000b0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
