\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Shouldn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  To Protect Rupee - Former Finance Ministry Adviser\b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2011\par 06:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Former Finance Ministry Adviser: RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be at odds with goals of monetary policy\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Shouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect rupee - Former Finance Ministry Adviser\par \par \uc2 By Sudeep Jain\par \par \uc2 Of Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to protect the rupee as it would go against the goals of monetary policy, a former adviser to India's finance ministry said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  should focus on using its monetary policy tools to stabilize the domestic economy rather than try to manage the exchange rate, Ajay Shah, who advised India's \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  between 2001 and 2005, told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 Shah, currently a professor at the National Institute for Public Finance and Policy in New Delhi, has served on a number of RBI committees and has authored several research papers on capital flows, exchange-rate policy and monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 His views are watched by the market.\par \par \uc2 His comments are at odds with increasing calls from Indian companies for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to protect the rupee, which fell to a fresh record low against the U.S. dollar Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar has gained about 19% since March against the local unit, which has been hit by souring sentiment toward risk-sensitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to Europe's sovereign debt crisis, coupled with concerns about India's high inflation, slowing economic growth and rising risk of the budget deficit widening.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been light so far, and it has instead taken a host of measures to boost foreign capital portfolio inflows such as increasing the limits on foreign investment in local debt, and easing rules on overseas borrowing and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap hedges by Indian companies.\par \par \uc2 But in recent days, the RBI has struck a tougher note on the rupee, saying it will use all possible measures, including strategic capital controls, if the risk of the rupee depreciating escalates.\par \par \uc2 However, Shah said the RBI should allow the exchange rate to float freely, and communicate its stance clearly so that Indian companies don't pin their hopes on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect them from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations.\par \par \uc2 "We cannot simultaneously have an open capital account, an exchange rate policy and an autonomous monetary policy. Now that we have an open capital account, we have to chose between the other two," he said.\par \par \uc2 Shah said that the current phase of intolerably high inflation has its roots in the RBI's attempt to prevent the rupee's appreciation by buying U.S. dollars in the first half of the previous decade, thereby flooding the domestic market with liquidity.\par \par \uc2 "We lost control of inflation because we targeted the exchange rate," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased its key policy rate 13 times in about 20 months to tame inflation that has remained above 9% for 11 months through October.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   --By Sudeep Jain, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 6145 6123; sudeep.jain@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 13-12-11 0540GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111213e7cd0008j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
