\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee hits new record low;more weakness seen\b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2011\par 12:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee touches all time low of 53.52/dollar\par \par \uc2 * Economic outlook, risk aversion weigh on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * May hit 55/dollar in coming sessions - traders\par \par \uc2 By Aditya Phatak\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Dec 13 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee touched a record low for the second day in a row on Tuesday as both foreign and domestic investors snapped up dollars to reduce exposure to India's cooling economy.\par \par \uc2 A firmer stock market provided a bit of comfort, but traders said the rupee looks to be headed lower still as worries about the euro crisis add to anxiety about slowing foreign capital inflows into emerging market economies such as India.\par \par \uc2 A growing trade deficit and the low probability of strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the limited firepower in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, is likely to keep the rupee under pressure, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 53.22/23 to the dollar, down 0.7 percent from Monday's close of 52.84/85, after touching a record low of 53.52 during the day.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 4.8 percent of its value against the dollar in the last four weeks and 16 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Investors took fright on Monday when government data showed India's industrial production fell 5.1 percent in October, the first monthly fall in more two years and far more than expected.\par \par \uc2 "The (industrial output) data has given a bad impression about India's growth outlook," said Uday Bhatt, senior manager of dealing at \uc2 UCO Bank\uc2 . "The current account and fiscal deficit are adding to the negative view," said Bhatt, who expects the rupee to fall to 54.50 in coming sessions.\par \par \uc2 Some traders believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon could weaken to 55 to the dollar within days.\par \par \uc2 "Any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the RBI is likely to be token," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a private-sector bank. "The one factor that could help rupee to some extent is growth-supporting steps from the RBI, like a cut in the cash reserve ratio."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to keep rates on hold at its review on Friday, but economists in a Reuters poll expect it to accelerate monetary easing in 2012 as economic conditions worsen in Asia's third-largest economy. (For details of the poll, click on ).\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts were quoted at 53.68, lower than the onshore spot rate indicating a bearish outlook.\par \par \uc2 The one-month onshore forward dollar premium was at 33.50 points, up from 33.25 on Monday. The three-month was at 79.50, up from 75 and the one-year premium was at 225.75, up from 216.50.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, the most traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX, and the United Stock Exchange ended at 53.4250, 53.4200 and 53.4150, respectively. Total volume was $6.12 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Ted Kerr)\par \par \uc2 INDIA/RUPEE(UPDATE 2) (REPEAT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111216e7cd000oe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
