\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's Gokarn: To Use All Steps If  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Risk Mounts\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2011\par 12:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --India \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to use all possible steps including capital controls if rupee depreciation risk escalates\par \par \uc2 --RBI's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to address short-term rupee risk, medium-term external obligations\par \par \uc2 (Updates with official's comments, background, beginning in third paragraph) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Eric Yep \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  will use all possible measures at its disposal including strategic capital controls if the risk of the rupee depreciating escalates, its deputy governor Subir Gokarn said Saturday, hinting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could now \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to calm a jittery local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rupee has weakened nearly 17% against the U.S. dollar since April, making it the worst-performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia, but the RBI has mostly refrained from major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the fall so far.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Resisting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation is best done by increasing the supply of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and by expanding market participation," Gokarn said at a conference.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, in the current volatile market conditions, RBI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep markets orderly and prevent a downward spiral of the rupee is justified, Gokarn said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Our broad objective in such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is to ensure that we find a balance between the short-term risk of the rupee spiraling downward and the medium-term risk of a loss of confidence in our ability to meet our external obligations," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gokarn said the RBI has instruments in the form of capital controls which can be used to enhance supply of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "These will be used when appropriate with the goal of ensuring that the availability of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does not become a destabilizing constraint," Gokarn said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RBI officials previously have said selling dollars to aggressively defend the rupee would drain India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, which provide an essential cushion against the country's external liabilities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves stood at $314.339 billion as of Nov. 11.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , instead of heavily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market so far, has recently taken a host of measures to boost overseas capital inflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It eased rules on overseas borrowing by Indian firms, raised the cap on the total cost of some of those loans, and also eased rules on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -swap hedges by companies to help them cope with exchange-rate volatility.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also raised the cap on interest rates banks can pay nonresident Indian depositors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gokarn said the bank's "strategic behavior should not be misconstrued as the inability to lean against the wind" and if it sees an increasing risk of a downward spiral in the rupee it will "not be hesitant to use all available instruments."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If the risk of a spiral escalates we can and will respond but we may have to recognize that volatility will be with us for a while and we will have to deal with it," Gokarn said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Eric Yep, Dow Jones Newswires; 91-11-43563301; abhrajit.gangopadhyay@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 03, 2011 06:36 ET (11:36 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111203e7c3000kv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
