\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cenbanker: seeking 'balancing act' with  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2011\par 04:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story issued late on Wednesday)\par \par \uc2 PARIS, Nov 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth sharp movements in the rupee and prevent a downward spiral in its value, but will balance this with the need to retain reserves in the event of prolonged turbulence, its deputy head said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Subir Gokarn, a deputy governor of the Reserve Bank of India, said the bank was not targeting a specific exchange rate with its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Indian rupee slid to an all-time low of 52.73 against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday but bounced back more than 1 percent on Wednesday after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The response is really...trying to remove sharp movements. That is the kind of technical and judgement criteria we used when we decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but that has not been with the objective of targeting a rate," Gokarn told reporters in Paris.\par \par \uc2 "We need to balance out the short-term risk of an uncontrolled spiral (in the rupee) with the medium-term risk of ensuring that we have adequate reserves to deal with a potentially prolonged market turbulence," he said. "Our approach to the rupee is going to be determined by this balancing act."\par \par \uc2 He said administrative and capital flow measures to ease overseas borrowing rules for corporates announced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday were part of its broader approach.\par \par \uc2 "These are certainly measures which will support the pricing, and will take some of that spiral risk out of the picture but we will have to continuously monitor the situation and make judgements about where the risks are heading," he said.\par \par \uc2 The rupee is under pressure as foreign investors are paring their exposure to Asia's third-largest economy amid global uncertainty and mounting worries over the domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has lost around 14 percent of its value in 2011 to be the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia.\par \par \uc2 For more news on the rupee, see.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting By Daniel Flynn; Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-ECONOMY/CENBANKDEPUTY(URGENT) (REPEAT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111127e7bo00022\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
