\par\par \b \uc2 EXCLUSIVE-UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  finmin against 'undue'  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  mkt  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -source\b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2011\par 08:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupee seen at around 50 to a dollar for 3 months: fin min source\par \par \uc2 * Government taking measures to increase capital flows: fin min source\par \par \uc2 * Rupee has slipped around 14 percent in 2011: fin min source\par \par \uc2 * July-September GDP growth seen below 7 pct\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Manoj Kumar\par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI, Nov 23 (Reuters) - India's finance ministry is not in favour of any "undue" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the rupee, a senior finance ministry source told Reuters on Wednesday, a day after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record low against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Economic growth in second quarter could be slightly less than 7 percent, the source said, adding that growth could pick up in the third and fourth quarter and end the fiscal year at around 7.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 The government will release official figures of GDP for the second quarter ending September next week.\par \par \uc2 The rupee on Tuesday slid to an all-time low of 52.73 against the U.S. dollar as foreign investors continued to pare their exposure to Asia's third-largest economy on lingering global uncertainty and mounting worries over the domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has lost 14 percent of its value in 2011 to be the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia.\par \par \uc2 "We are not in favour of undue \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank except to check volatility, because of macro-economic implications for the next year," the source, who declined to be named, said.\par \par \uc2 "The rupee is depreciating mainly because of external reasons which are outside our control."\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, bounced back more than 1 percent on Wednesday after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The comments endorse the stand taken by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI)\uc2 , which has always maintained that it does not protect any particular level of the rupee and would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to iron out excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  operates independently on monetary issues but often consults the government on important policy moves.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the rupee to remain around 50 for next three months," the source said.\par \par \uc2 "It should firm up to around 45 over a period of 5-6 months...if the situation in the euro zone does not deteriorate."\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee on Tuesday also blamed the fall in the rupee on the international market and said that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have a limited effect.\par \par \uc2 Subir Gokarn, a deputy governor at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had said last week the RBI would be careful about using \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves aggressively to protect the rupee's depreciation..\par \par \uc2 At 11:30 a.m. (0600 GMT), the rupee was trading at 52.02/03, 0.5 percent stronger than 52.2950/3050 at close on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have sold more than $500 million worth of shares over five trading sessions till Monday, reducing the net inflows in 2011 to under $300 million, sharply below record investments of more than $29 billion seen in 2010.\par \par \uc2 The official said New Delhi is taking measures to revive business sentiments and attract capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 The government has already raised ownership limits on government and corporate bonds and is considering allowing international retail investors direct access to Indian stocks , which have slumped about 22 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 It is also considering allowing foreign direct investment in the country's struggling domestic airlines.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Manoj Kumar; editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/FINMIN (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111126e7bn00055\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
