\par\par \b \uc2 SNAPSHOT-Indian policy highlights on Tuesday, Nov. 8\b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2011\par 11:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Nov 8 (Reuters) - Following are statements from Indian policymakers as well as the latest news and scheduled events.\par \par \uc2 * Denotes new entry.\par \par \uc2 * India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stick to its exchange rate policy and the guidance provided on monetary policy would hold until further notice, a deputy governor at the bank, Subir Gokarn, said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "We have repeatedly said that the rupee is now a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the boundaries of the regime of structural capital controls on debt inflows," Gokarn told reporters at a televised event.\par \par \uc2 "There is no intent to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a particular exchange rate target in mind."\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  could decide whether to allow more sugar exports at a meeting of a panel of ministers likely to be on Nov. 16 or 17, Food Minister K.V. Thomas said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "We have worked out a scheme for exports of a certain quantity of sugar. I had a wider discussion with (Farm Minister Sharad) Pawar on sugar production. We have more or less agreed on exporting a certain quantity," Thomas said.\par \par \uc2 CONTEXT NEWS\par \par \uc2 * The partially convertible rupee has been the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia so far this year, having shed more than 9 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  raised interest rates in late October for the 13th and possibly final time in a tightening cycle that began in early 2010, on expectations that persistently high inflation will finally begin to ease starting in December.\par \par \uc2 * India is the world's top consumer of the sweetener but also produces enough to give it space for exports currently.\par \par \uc2 It is the world's-second biggest producer of the sweetener after Brazil and exported 2.6 million tonnes in 2010/11.\par \par \uc2 Industry and analysts say India could decide to allow 500,000 tonnes of exports in a first tranche but delay further quantities until early 2012 due to output delays.\par \par \uc2 SCHEDULED EVENTS THIS WEEK:\par \par \uc2 THURSDAY, Nov. 10\par \par \uc2 ---------------------\par \par \uc2 Stocks, bonds, rupee and commodities markets shut for Gurunanak Jayanti holiday\par \par \uc2 Data: Weekly food inflation data at around noon (0630 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Weekly data on water level in 81 main reservoirs \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par         \tab \par FRIDAY, Nov. 11    \tab \par ---------------------    \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data: Weekly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves data at 5 p.m. IST (1130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Weekly bank credit data\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Compiled by Annie Banerji in NEW DELHI)\f28 \par \par \uc2 INDIA-POLICY/SNAPSHOT   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111111e7b80018z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
