\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-India cbank: plcy guidance to hold for now-TV\b0\par\par\uc2 392 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2011\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Exchange rate policy remains unchanged - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  cbank deputy\par \par \uc2 * Do not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with any particular target in mind\par \par \uc2 * Plcy guidance to hold until further notice\par \par \uc2 (Updates with quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 Nov 8 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stick to its exchange rate policy and the guidance provided on monetary policy would hold until further notice, a deputy governor at the bank, Subir Gokarn, said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "We have repeatedly said that the rupee is now a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the boundaries of the regime of structural capital controls on debt inflows," Gokarn told reporters at a televised event.\par \par \uc2 "There is no intent to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a particular exchange rate target in mind."\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee has been the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia so far this year, having shed more than 9 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Gokarn said that the rupee's losses are due to global conditions and capital reallocations around the world have impacted many \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  raised interest rates in late October for the 13th and possibly final time in a tightening cycle that began in early 2010, on expectations that persistently high inflation will finally begin to ease starting in December.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was unlikely to raise rates again in December and may remain on hold subsequently if inflation follows its projected trajectory.\par \par \uc2 "We gave the guidance two weeks ago. If we want to change the guidance we will change the guidance...Unless there is something dramatic that happens to change it, that guidance remains. So let us say, the guidance remains the same until further notice at this stage," Gokarn said.\par \par \uc2 Government-backed fuel retailers have raised gasoline prices by about 2.7 percent from Friday. The move, aimed at cutting revenue losses of oil firms, is likely to add pressure to stubbornly high inflation in Asia's third-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 RBI may consider reversing its tight monetary stance as inflationary woes begin to ebb next month, a top policy adviser said on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only consider easing monetary policy if inflation falls below 7 percent, Governor Duvvuri Subbarao had said a day after its policy review on Oct. 25.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Swati Bhat; Editing by Subhadip Sircar)\par \par \uc2 INDIA-CBANK/GOKARN  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111111e7b8000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
