\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee drops 1 pct on euro zone worries\b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2011\par 06:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * May touch 49.90/dlr, matching 28-mo low hit on Sept. 23-traders\par \par \uc2 * Sept factory output growth slows sharply; shares fall 2 pct\par \par \uc2 * Euro hits 8-month low after Greece likely to miss deficit target\par \par \uc2 (Updates to mid-morning)\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 3 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee shed more than 1 percent on Monday as deepening concerns over impact of Europe's debt crisis on global growth pummeled domestic shares and the euro.\par \par \uc2 Manufacturing growth in India nearly stalled in September, hitting its weakest spot since March 2009 on slowing output and orders growth following a series of rate hikes, a survey showed.\par \par \uc2 The data from \uc2 HSBC\uc2  Markit suggest that September was the worst month for India's factories since March 2009 -- when it shrank, just as world stock markets carved their lowest point since the financial crisis began.\par \par \uc2 At 11:16 a.m. (0546 GMT), the partially convertible rupee\par \par \uc2 was 49.41/42 per dollar, 0.9 percent weaker than its previous close of 48.97/98. It had touched 49.57 in early trade.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the rupee could slide to 49.90, matching a 28-month low hit on Sept. 23, if risk aversion continues to dominate world markets. The 30-share BSE index fell nearly 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 "If the euro continues to slip the way it has in the past few sessions, then rupee may well hit 49.90 again," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a private-sector bank.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suspected to have sold dollars when the rupee had touched that level in September, and traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hopes would keep the unit from slipping to 50.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 releases \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data with a lag and the September action will be known in November.\par \par \uc2 On Sept. 28, H.R. Khan, one of the deputy governors of the RBI, had told Reuters in Istanbul that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monitors domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movement closely and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "smooth excess volatility whenever there is need".\par \par \uc2 The euro sank to an eight-month low against the dollar on Monday and is poised to fall further after the Greek government said the debt-ridden country will miss a deficit target set just months ago in a massive bailout package.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.3331, sharply lower from $1.3614 at the end of rupee trade last week, while the index of the dollar\par \par \uc2 against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at 79.056 points from 77.721 previously.\par \par \uc2 The one-month onshore forward premium was at 25.25 points from 21.75, the three-month was at 63.75 points from 62 and the one-year was at 125.75 points from 125.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were quoted at 49.68, weaker than the spot rate and indicating a bearish medium-term outlook.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market , the most traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and on the United Stock Exchange were all at 49.62. The total traded volume on the three exchanges was $1.7 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Aditya Phatak; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111006e7a30005e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
