\par\par \b \uc2 RBI FOCUS- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  wary of losing dlrs, prefers modest  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 979 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2011\par 08:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Current account deficit, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are key concerns\par \par \uc2  * Rupee still undervalued in trade-weighted terms\par \par \uc2  * Impact on inflation in case of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only incidental \par \par \uc2  By Suvashree Dey Choudhury and Aditya Phatak\par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Sept 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a big way in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, unlike most of its emerging Asian peers, because it can ill-afford to expend a limited and fragile holding of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources say.\par \par \uc2  That reluctance to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  is just one of the factors that sets the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  apart. It also is currently the most hawkish in the region, waging an expensive and tough war against inflation, while most of the world frets about slowing U.S. growth and a European debt crisis.\par \par \uc2  A persistent current account deficit and realisation that an uncertain global environment is bound to keep markets volatile are reasons the RBI is loath to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a big way, spending its small pool of dollar reserves, sources with direct knowledge of the matter told Reuters.\par \par \uc2  While many Asian central banks including South Korea, Indonesia and Philippines have been spotted selling dollars to protect their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the RBI has put up only a token show, with some minor \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's partially convertible rupee has been the worst performer among major Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- so far in 2011, losing nearly 12 percent of its value since touching its 2011 high of 43.855 against the dollar on July 27.\par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  depends upon the pace of volatility. But the threshold for volatility also changes with the situation," an official familiar with the matter told Reuters.\par \par \uc2  "Look at how the euro has been behaving, how gold, U.S. Treasuries have been moving. If all asset classes are so volatile, then the tolerance level will also rise."\par \par \uc2  The rupee has weakened nearly 7.2 percent against the dollar since late August, on heightened concerns over European sovereign debt and a likely Greece default. The euro\par \par \uc2 has fallen on most days since Aug. 29, 7.3\par \par \uc2 percent down in the period and touched a seven-month low of $1.3499 on Sept. 12.\par \par \uc2  In the same period, the key Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 --Korean won\par \par \uc2 , Indonesian rupiah , Philippine peso have\par \par \uc2 fallen between 1 percent and 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  UNDERVALUED\par \par \uc2  The RBI's modest approach would be understandable if they were keeping the rupee stable in trade-weighted terms, but that is not the case. The rupee has been increasingly undervalued in nominal trade-weighted terms.\par \par \uc2  However, this approach is not new. Its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has by definition been hands off.\par \par \uc2  Asia's third largest economy has reserves that are merely a tenth of the size of mighty neighbour China's. Because India runs a trade deficit, the reserves also comprise a pool of borrowed money that can dwindle quickly should foreigners pull short-term investments away from the country.\par \par \uc2  Still, many traders and economists are now questioning the wisdom of sticking to that practice amid high inflation, a large trade deficit and heightened uncertainty across \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2  "Downside pressure remains strong, and one-off \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be enough in an environment of growing contagion risks. This begs the question of whether an increase in the frequency and magnitude of RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely," Standard Chartered said in a report. \par \par \uc2  The RBI was last a net seller of dollars in April 2009, when the Lehman crisis weakened the rupee, and any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since then has always been aimed at checking a rise in the local unit.\par \par \uc2 But the biggest impediment to dollar sales is the country's current account deficit , a stark contrast with its Asian peers such as Indonesia, South Korea and Taiwan, all of whom are running current account surpluses.  \par \par \uc2  "There is an asymmetry when a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and when it sells dollars to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the official familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2  "When you are selling dollars, you are losing the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which is not a very comfortable thought given that we are a current account deficit country." \par \par \uc2  In the face of foreign fund outflows and India's trade deficit, the RBI's absence from the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has only fuelled investor pessimism towards the rupee, the Standard Chartered economists noted.\par \par \uc2  India's current account deficit in January-March narrowed to $5.4 billion from $12.8 billion deficit a year earlier, but the global slowdown could hurt exports, widening the deficit again.\par \par \uc2  A wider current account deficit would put pressure on the country's ability to buy oil which is by far the largest component in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's import bill. \par \par \uc2  INFLATION AND \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Though the RBI maintains that it will never use the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to contain inflation, selling dollars to arrest the rupee's current sharp drop has the added attraction of helping to ease imported inflation.\par \par \uc2  India's big state oil companies last week raised the price of petrol by nearly 5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Yes, the petrol prices were raised because of the rupee depreciation and not due to any rise in global oil prices and that will have an impact on inflation," said another official senior official, directly involved in the matter.\par \par \uc2  "But any impact on inflation due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be incidental and not our objective," the official added.\par \par \uc2  India's headline inflation has stayed over 9 percent for the last four months and persistently above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comfort zone of 4.0-4.5 percent despite the RBI's aggressive 18-month rate tightening cycle.\par \par \uc2  "It is a sentiment spiral that started in August and I don't think the rupee will turn around unless there is some positive development globally," he added. \par \par \uc2 (Editing by Tony Munroe and Vidya Ranganathan)\par \par \uc2 RBI-FOCUS/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110926e79n000bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\