\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee falls to new 28-mo low; cbank moves watched\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2011\par 04:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker against dlr, weighs on rupee\par \par \uc2 * Indian shares in red, pulls rupee down\par \par \uc2 * Traders eyeing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 23 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee extended losses on Friday to slide to a fresh 28-month low as demand for dollars persisted in a risk-averse environment, with traders watching for any possible move by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the unit's fall.\par \par \uc2 At 11:19 a.m. (0549 GMT), the partially convertible rupee\par \par \uc2 was at 49.77/79 per dollar, after falling to 49.90, its weakest since May 14, 2009. It had slumped 2.5 percent on Thursday to 49.57/58, its lowest close since May 15, 2009.\par \par \uc2 "There is a lot of demand for dollars and RBI is the most important factor to see as to where they will come and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader with a private bank.\par \par \uc2 "I think we can slowly go towards 50 levels if RBI does not come."\par \par \uc2 A state-run bank dealer said there could be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 around 49.90 levels.\par \par \uc2 RBI deputy governor Subir Gokarn, in an interview with a television channel, said that any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be only be to smoothen volatility and not to target any particular level.\par \par \uc2 The RBI was suspected to be selling dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday at around 49.15 rupees, traders said, but the selling pressure on the rupee was too high for it to contain the drop.\par \par \uc2 Indian shares fell more than 1 percent, adding to the previous session's large losses, as prospect of a global recession hit world markets.\par \par \uc2 Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also weaker against the dollar. For a snapshot, see\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.3481, marginally higher than $1.3456 at end of rupee trade on Wednesday, while the index of the dollar against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at 78.345 points from 78.506 previously.\par \par \uc2 The world's major economies pledged on Thursday to prevent Europe's debt crisis from undermining banks and financial markets, and said the euro zone's rescue fund would be bolstered.\par \par \uc2 However, dealers said the mild gains in the euro was unlikely to aid the rupee.\par \par \uc2 "I doubt it will help, given the risk aversion. Also, equities are in minus," a trader with a state-run bank said.\par \par \uc2 The one-month onshore forward premium was at 21.75 points from 21 on Thursday, the three-month was at 66.75 points from 63 and the one-year was at 132.25 points from 126.50.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were quoted at 50.11, weaker than the onshore spot rate.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market , the most traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange and the MCX-SX were at 49.8200 and the United Stock Exchange were at 49.8175. The total volume was $3.9 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Shamik Paul; Editing by Subhadip Sircar)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110926e79n0004p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
