\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: India  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Panel Member: Weak Rupee Reflects Market Forces\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2011\par 15:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Rupee responding to demand and supply - Member of policy advisory panel\par \par \uc2 -- No indication of significant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers\par \par \uc2 -- Dollar could breach INR50 if no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - Standard Chartered\par \par \uc2 -- RBI will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when situation warrants - Finance minister\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from traders in 3rd paragraph, panel member in 5th paragraph, finance minister in 6th paragraph, analysts in 10th and 12th-13th paragraphs; context and background.)\par \par \uc2 By Abhrajit Gangopadhyay & Bijou George\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--The current bout of weakness in the Indian rupee reflects "market forces at this moment" as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "responding to demand and supply," said Shankar Acharya, a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advisory panel on monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Acharya's comments came even as the rupee slipped to a more than 28-month low against the U.S. dollar Thursday, as investors sold off risk-sensitive assets after the U.S. Federal Reserve late Wednesday signaled sustained weakness in the economy and tinkered with its portfolio maturities rather than plunging into a fresh round of bond buying.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shied away from any meaningful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local unit. "There have been enquiries from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but no clear indication of a large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a state-run bank.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's stated stance is its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be to curb volatility, and not to protect a specific level.\par \par \uc2 The present \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor is less prone to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market than his predecessor, Acharya said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "as and when the situation warrants," but there is no such situation at present, according to a Press Trust of India report.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has been among the most vulnerable of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to risk aversion this year.\par \par \uc2 Acharya said India stands out for its combination of stubborn inflation and high current-account and fiscal deficits, factors that affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These factors have been increasingly deterring foreign investors, who have pulled out more than $2 billion from local stocks in August alone, according to data from the securities regulator.\par \par \uc2 If the RBI doesn't come up with a decisive action, the rupee may weaken further and the dollar could rise above the key INR50.00 level, said Priyanka Kishore, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered Bank.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading INR49.57 late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "If the drop in the rupee becomes too extreme, the RBI may be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets or take other measures to limit speculative trading in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mitul Kotecha, a global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  CIB. "Other countries have implemented various restrictions on the use of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the RBI may choose to emulate these if market volatility gets out of hand."\par \par \uc2 Kotecha expects the dollar to slip to INR45.40 by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 -By Abhrajit Gangopadhyay & Bijou George, Dow Jones Newswires; 91-11-43563301 abhrajit.gangopadhyay@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Anant Vijay Kala contributed to this report [ 22-09-11 1348GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110922e79m0012b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
