\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee posts biggest single day fall in 3 years\b0\par\par\uc2 722 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2011\par 15:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected; fails to support unit-traders\par \par \uc2 * Rupee sheds 2.5 percent; weakest in more than 28 months\par \par \uc2 * Local equities dive 4.1 percent; biggest fall in 2 years\par \par \uc2 * More weakness in rupee likely on risk off mood - \uc2 HDFC Bank\par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Aditya Phatak\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee suffered its biggest single session fall in nearly three years on Thursday after a grim outlook on the U.S. economy sent investors scrambling for safer \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government bonds.\par \par \uc2 Signs that growth in China and Germany could be slowing down added to the global risk sell off, with local equities posting their biggest one-day drop in more than two-years.\par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to be selling dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday at around 49.15 rupees, traders said, but the selling pressure on the rupee was too high for it to contain the drop.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 49.57/58 to a dollar, 2.5 percent lower from its previous close, and its lowest since May 15, 2009.\par \par \uc2 The unit's fall is the largest single day fall since Nov. 12, 2008 when it dropped 2.6 percent during the peak of the global financial crisis post the \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  bankruptcy.\par \par \uc2 "It is difficult to take a view on future rupee levels currently as it is being driven by sentiment currently. And so long as the risk aversion mood remains, rupee will continue to be under pressure," said \uc2 Ashish Parthasarthy\uc2 , treasurer at \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Parthasarthy added active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was needed to help subside the panic and "smoothen any wrinkles" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The steep fall in the rupee will also add pressure on inflation as India imports more than 80 percent of its oil requirements.\par \par \uc2 "With this rupee weakness to two year low is expected to add up to the inflationary figures putting further pressure on the economy," said D.K. Aggarwal, chief managing director of SMC Investments and Advisors Ltd.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell to a fresh eight month low against the dollar on Thursday a day after the Federal Reserve pointed to significant downside risks for the U.S. economy and stopped short of bold monetary easing.\par \par \uc2 The was at $1.3456 at end of rupee trade from $1.3652 on Wednesday, while the index of the dollar against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 78.506 points from 77.248 previously.\par \par \uc2 A bulletin released by the RBI on Sept. 13 showed it had not bought or sold dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in July, for the eight successive month.\par \par \uc2 The RBI's hands-off policy may have made the unit more vulnerable during periods of risk aversion, a note by Standard Chartered Bank research note on Wednesday said.\par \par \uc2 Despite the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  being the worst performer so far this year amongst major Asian peers, losing nearly 10 percent against the greenback, some traders believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may rebound going ahead.\par \par \uc2 "The current bout of weakness in rupee is a short-term phenomenon. Once clarity on growth in euro zone and the United States returns, monies will flow thick and fast into India where fundamentals for growth are still in place," said N.S. Venkatesh, treasurer at \uc2 IDBI Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the mid-quarter review on Sept. 16, the RBI kept its projection of GDP growth for the country in the current financial year unchanged at 8 percent.\par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have bought $485 million of local equities so far this month after having sold $2.2 billion in August\par \par \uc2 The one-month onshore forward premium was at 21 points from 17.50 on Wednesday, the three-month was at 63 points from 50.75 and the one-year was at 126.5 points from 114.75.\par \par \uc2 The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were quoted at 49.91, weaker than the onshore spot rate.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market , the most traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange ended at 49.6700, 49.6500 and 49.6300 respectively. The total volume was $12.73 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Aradhana Aravindan)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/   (REPEAT) (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110925e79m000ci\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
