\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ UPDATE: Global Fears Drag Indian Rupee Lower\b0\par\par\uc2 508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2011\par 14:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Indian rupee at lowest level vs. U.S. dollar in more than two years\par \par \uc2 --Calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --Rupee closed at 49.56, down 1.23 rupees\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Shefali Anand \par    Of THE WALL STREET JOURNAL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Updates with the closing value of the Indian rupee.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee fell to its lowest level against the U.S. dollar in more than two years on Thursday, with many \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders and economists clamoring for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the partially convertible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decline.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Thursday, the rupee fell 1.23 rupees to close at INR49.56 to the U.S. dollar because of increasing nervousness globally about a potential default in Europe. The rupee has now weakened more than 10% this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee's decline on Thursday was accompanied by sharp losses in the Indian stock market which tracked other Asian markets lower. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bombay Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Sensitive Index fell 704 points or 4.13% to close at 16,361.15.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A key reason for the rupee's sharp decline in recent weeks has been the inability of Indian companies and other agencies which borrow abroad to roll over some of their debt, because foreign banks have been reluctant to lend lately. So these companies have had to pay off their foreign loans, leading to a sell-off in Indian rupees. "It's not an India-specific problem," said Sujan Hajra, chief economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anand Rathi Financial Services Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, global investors have also pulled some of their money out of India, selling rupees. Foreign institutional investors have pulled out $200 million from the Indian stock market since last Monday, according to data from the Securities and Exchange Board of India.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This story and related background material will be available on The Wall Street Journal website, WSJ.com.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The weakening rupee could exacerbate India's already difficult inflation picture. Despite a series of interest-rate increases designed to staunch inflation, it remains stubbornly high and well outside the RBI's comfort zone.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A weakening rupee "raises the inflation almost automatically," said Abheek Barua, chief economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 HDFC Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Most commodities imported by India, particularly oil, are denominated in dollars making these expensive for India.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Recently, some car companies which import some of their components said they might raise their prices if the rupee continues to weaken.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The major beneficiaries of a falling rupee would be India's exporters and to some extent India's information technology industry, which earns a majority of its income in the U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 So far the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which has the power to buy rupees and boost its value, has stayed on the sidelines, but industry experts would like it to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The rupee uncertainty has added to the uncertainty of the underlying equity markets," said Barua, which in turn could scare foreign investors away.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Shefali Anand, The Wall Street Journal; 011919717764577 [ 09-22-11 0800ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110922e79m0003d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
