\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Rupee depreciation short term, no need for  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  official\b0\par\par\uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2011\par 04:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Repeats story issued late on Wednesday)\par \par \uc2  * Rupee plunges to near 2-yr low of 48.02/dlr in early trade\par \par \uc2  * Some dealers believe cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot market-TV reports\par \par \uc2  * Fin min meet on Thursday may raise overseas debt cap: source \par \par \uc2  By Rajesh Kumar Singh\par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee's depreciation is only a short-term disruption which does not require \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a senior official in \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 has always maintained that it does not target any specific exchange rate and only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent excessive volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2  The RBI has stayed away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for\par \par \uc2 eight straight months until August, its monthly bulletin showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2  The partially convertible rupee ended at 47.62/63 to a dollar, weaker from Tuesday's close of 47.59/60, but off its intraday low of 48.02, a level last seen on Sept. 29, 2009.\par \par \uc2 Worries Europe's debt problems may snowball into a banking crisis roiled global markets and pushed investors to the dollar's perceived safety and also weighed on the rupee.\par \par \uc2  "This is something that is a very short period kind of disruption. So I don't think we need to give up a policy for short-term disruption," R. Gopalan, the economic affairs secretary at the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told reporters.\par \par \uc2  However, some market participants said the RBI may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday to arrest a sharp fall.\par \par \uc2  TV reports however had quoted some sources as saying that the RBI had not stepped in to protect the rupee. Dealers said the rupee's recovery was mostly driven by euro and some dollar inflows.\par \par \uc2  The rupee has shed 8.7 percent since its highest level of 43.855 to the dollar, reached on July 27 this year.\par \par \uc2  "The rupee has underperformed especially as dollars have been pulled out of Asia and India to safe havens outside, so it could slip to 48.5 or even 48.8 as early as next week before it stabilises," said Jonathan Cavenagh, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac Institutional Bank in Singapore.\par \par \uc2  Any sharp fall in the rupee will inflate India's import bill, as oil accounts for more than 80 percent of the country's total imports.\par \par \uc2  Benchmark Brent crude futures <LCOc1> was trading at around $112 per barrel by 0857 GMT, coming off from its $116 per barrel perch at the beginning of August, weighed by concerns on the fragile outlook for the United States and the euro zone.\par \par \uc2  However, a depreciating rupee could nullify the advantage.\par \par \uc2  Gopalan admitted as much and said that a weak rupee will push up the cost of Indian imports but endorsed the RBI's stated position of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets unless it is forced to smooth out volatility.\par \par \uc2  "I think the RBI is following a good policy by not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2  So far in 2011, the rupee has depreciated by around 6.5 percent and is the worst performer among its Asian peers.\par \par \uc2  "There cannot be much that can be done about the rupee depreciation situation right now," said Kaushik Basu, the chief economic adviser to the finance ministry.\par \par \uc2  If the depreciation in the rupee continues for long, it could inflate India's trade deficit and put pressure on the current account deficit.\par \par \uc2  With demand holding up in some quarters, Indian imports\par \par \uc2 grew about 42 percent in August while trade deficit stood at $14.1 billion, provisional trade figures released by  Trade Secretary Rahul Khullar last week showed. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that the medium-term outlook for the rupee on a 6-12 month horizon could be around 44 to the dollar level, but only if the global economic outlook improves.\par \par \uc2  Separately, sources in the finance ministry said a meeting on Thursday will decide on raising the limit on overseas borrowing, which is currently at $30 billion. The meeting is also expected to decide on allowing overseas debt in yuan. \par \par \uc2 (Writing by Abhijit Neogy; editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -RUPEE/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (REPEAT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110918e79f0003f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
