\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee hits near 9-month low on importer dlr demand\b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2011\par 05:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Oil companies step up dollar buying for Iran payments\par \par \uc2  * Strong Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , local shares may arrest fall\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , say traders\par \par \uc2  * Rupee seen in 45.90-46.15/dlr range intraday \par \par \uc2 (Updates to mid-morning)\par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Aug 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee touched its weakest level in nearly nine months on Monday, dragged by dollar demand from domestic oil refiners for import payments as well as bunched up outflows following last Friday's local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond markets holiday.\par \par \uc2  But any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the rupee was unlikely unless the unit weakened sharply from the current level, traders said.\par \par \uc2  Strong Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and local share gains, however, could underpin the local unit's sentiment, they added.\par \par \uc2  "It is too early to take a call on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It (rupee) did slide sharply at open, but has settled down after that. So unless we see a big drop from here...I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will let the rupee be," said a dealer with a private-sector bank.\par \par \uc2  The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 has maintained that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market only to reduce volatility.\par \par \uc2  At 11:41 a.m. (0612 GMT), the partially convertible rupee was at 45.96/97 per dollar, after dipping to 46.10, its weakest since Nov. 30. It had opened at 45.9250 after closing at 45.735/745 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2  "Oil payments are continuing. Rupee should see support around 46.15 level, mostly from exporters and resistance around 45.90," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a big private-sector bank.\par \par \uc2  Indian refiners will settle all oil debts to Iran by the end of this month, an Iranian business daily reported on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  New Delhi is estimated to owe around $5 billion to Tehran for its oil imports. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.4366 versus $1.4360 at end of domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, while the index of the dollar against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 74.066 points from 74.076 points previously.\par \par \uc2  For a snapshot of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , see \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 30-share main share index was up 0.04 percent in choppy trade after shedding nearly 2 percent on Friday.    \par \par \uc2  The one-month onshore forward premium was at 9 points from 7.50 points on Thursday, the three-month  was at 33.75 points from 30 and the one-year was at 139.50 points from 140.25.\par \par \uc2  The one-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts\par \par \uc2 were quoted at 46.105, weaker than the onshore spot rate.\par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market , the most traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, the MCX-SX and the United Stock Exchange were all at 45.9575. The total volume was at $3.35 billion. \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Aditya Phatak; editing by Malini Menon)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110825e78m0004n\par