\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cbank did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market in June\b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2011\par 09:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not buy or sell dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the seventh consecutive month in June, its monthly bulletin showed.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 has always maintained that it does not target any specific exchange rate and only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 The last time the RBI had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in November when it had bought $1.37 billion and sold $500 million, compared with purchases of $450 million in October.\par \par \uc2 On a net basis, that was the RBI's biggest monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since June 2009, when it had bought $1.04 billion.\par \par \uc2 The rupee moved in a band of 45.14 to 44.5750 per dollar in June.\par \par \uc2 In 2010, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net $1.85 billion, compared with net sales of $5.8 billion in 2009 when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the rupee from depreciating sharply.\par \par \uc2 The rupee had dropped to a record low of 52.2 in March 2009, but ended the year 4.7 percent higher, boosted by foreign fund inflows of $17.5 billion. In 2010, the rupee rose 4.1 percent, boosted by record inflows of $29.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 At 12:45 p.m. (0715 GMT) the partially convertible rupee was at 45.2850/2900 per dollar, 0.1 percent weaker than its previous close.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Neha D'Silva; Editing by Aradhana Aravindan)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 /   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110811e78b000pz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
