\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  cbank did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market in March\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2011\par 14:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, May 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not buy or sell dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the fourth straight month in March, its monthly bulletin showed, as the rupee had moved in a narrow band during the period, reducing the need for any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The last time the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \uc2 had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in November when it had bought $1.37 billion and sold $500 million, compared with purchases of $450 million in October.\par \par \uc2 On a net basis, November was the RBI's biggest monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since June 2009, when it had bought $1.04 billion.\par \par \uc2 The rupee moved in a narrow band of 44.52-45.38 per dollar in March.\par \par \uc2 The RBI has always maintained that it doesn't target any specific exchange rate level and only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors had bought around a net $2.5 billion of Indian shares in March, while they had dumped a net $826 million in February.\par \par \uc2 In 2010, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net $1.85 billion compared with net sales of $5.8 billion in 2009, when it had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the rupee from depreciating sharply.\par \par \uc2 The rupee had dropped to a record low of 52.2 per dollar in March 2009, but ended the year 4.7 percent higher, boosted by foreign fund inflows of $17.5 billion. In 2010, the rupee rose 4.1 percent, boosted by record inflows of $29.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 44.69/70 per dollar on Wednesday, stronger than its previous close of 44.74/75.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Suvashree Dey Choudhury; Editing by Aradhana Aravindan)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 /   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110511e75b0017b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
