\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: Indian  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Suspected To Have  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market - Traders\b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2011\par 14:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- Reserve Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  Suspected To Have Bought Dollars From INR43.98\par \par \uc2 -- Suspected RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  First Time Since November\par \par \uc2 -- Suspected RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Comes After Rupee Rises To Near-6-Month High\par \par \uc2 -- Rupee likely To Gain In Near Term, Tracking Euro - Banker\par \par \uc2 (Adds banker's comments and outlook on the rupee in paragraphs 7, 9 and 10, details throughout.)\par \par \uc2 By Anant Vijay Kala\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday after the rupee rose to a near-six-month high against the U.S. dollar, two traders said.\par \par \uc2 This is the first time since November that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market as the strengthening rupee threatens to hurt India's rapidly growing exports.\par \par \uc2 "There was substantial demand from nationalized banks," said a trader with a state-run bank, who didn't wish to be named. "This was believed to be on behalf of the RBI," he added.\par \par \uc2 Both traders said demand for the dollar was seen from around INR43.98, which was the intraday low for the dollar. The greenback had last fallen below this level in mid-October. It was trading at INR44.07 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 The dealers, however, declined to give an estimate on how much of the greenback the RBI may have bought.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had risen sharply early in the session after an interest rate hike by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Thursday fueled expectations of a similar action in India.\par \par \uc2 Sudarshana Bhat, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 Corporation Bank\uc2 , said the dollar's rebound was aided by demand from oil companies and weakening local stock markets.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bombay Stock Exchange\uc2 's benchmark Sensitive Index ended 0.7% lower at 19,451.40, down for a fourth consecutive session.\par \par \uc2 "But in the near-term, expectations are that the rupee will continue to strengthen tracking gains in the euro and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar," Bhat said.\par \par \uc2 The next crucial support for the pair will be at INR43.95. "If that is broken, then we could see the rupee gain all the way to INR43.75 or INR43.80 very soon," he added.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained 1.4% against the dollar so far in 2011 after rising about 4.0% the previous year.\par \par \uc2 The RBI has raised interest rates eight times since March 2010 as it struggles to control inflation. The markets widely expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would raise its main lending and borrowing rates by another 25 basis points when it next meets to review monetary policy on May 3.\par \par \uc2 The widening interest rate differential with advanced economies, which are still following loose growth-supportive policies, is attracting capital inflows into Asia's third-largest economy and in turn helping the rupee.\par \par \uc2 The RBI doesn't set a target level for the rupee and has often said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market only to curb excessive volatility.\par \par \uc2 -By Anant Vijay Kala, Dow Jones Newswires; +91-11-43563311; anant.kala@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 08, 2011 08:12 ET (12:12 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110408e748002o6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
