\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Singapore dlr, won lead gains; uptrend may persist\b0\par\par\uc2 1,255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2011\par 04:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Sing dlr at record high; MAS lets go of 1.2600/dlr\par \par \uc2  * Dlr/won hits 2-1/2-yr low; Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  at lower levels\par \par \uc2  * BNM lowers \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels to around 3.0220 \par \par \uc2 (Updates with text, prices)\par \par \uc2  By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 8 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar hit a record high and the South Korean won rose to a 2-1/2-year high on Friday, leading gains in emerging Asia, as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities pulled back their defence lines on domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength in the face of rising capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 The combination of robust equity flows into Asia and a revived interest in carry trades will probably keep emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthening in the near term, analysts and dealers said.\par \par \uc2  "Asian authorities have accepted that much of the gain in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to general U.S. dollar weakness whilst many central banks are allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do an increasing amount of the work to dampen inflation pressures," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Credit Agricole in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2  "Capital flows to Asia have strengthened sharply over recent weeks, pointing to ongoing upward momentum," he said, adding there is still risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation rather than reverse it.\par \par \uc2  Hedge funds piled on the move higher in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , taking particular interest in the Singapore dollar ahead of a policy meeting of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore next Thursday. MAS is widely expected to tighten policy, which it manages through exchange rates.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed investors to cross 1.2600 per dollar, which it had been defending. South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities had not been spotted buying dollars until the won hit a 2-1/2-year high beyond 1,085.00, having moved its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels increasingly lower in the past several weeks, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  Asian monetary authorities are facing a rising tide of portfolio investment entering their economies and putting upward pressure on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and also a risk of quickening inflation. Oil prices hit a 2-1/2-year high on Friday.\par \par \uc2  In the week ended Wednesday, emerging market equities enjoyed net inflows of $2.7 billion in fresh cash, the fourth-largest weekly tally since 1992, data from Lipper showed. [ID:nN07259168]\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The won hit a fresh 2-1/2-year high against the dollar as offshore hedge funds built up short yen/won and euro/won positions  .\par \par \uc2  The won strengthened to as firm as 1,082.0 versus the greenback during the local trade, the strongest since Sept. 8, 2008. Hedge funds had left dollar offers around 1,085 won, a U.S. bank dealer said.\par \par \uc2  The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  found further support from demand for exporters' settlements, while the authorities lowered their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level to 1,082 per dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors extended their net purchases of Seoul shares to a 18th consecutive session, helping the KOSPI  end up 0.27 percent. That is the longest string of net buying by foreign investors since October 2010.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar firmed to a record high of 1.2560 per U.S. dollar on surging demand after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed market players to cross the line which it had been defending.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) was seen pulling back dollar bids at 1.2600 per the greenback, although it was spotted buying it around 1.2560 later, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has been supported by expectations that the MAS will tighten more on Thursday to fight inflation.\par \par \uc2  YUAN NDFS\par \par \uc2  Dollar/yuan non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) fell sharply with the one-month NDF hitting a fresh all-time low, as investors rushed to catch up with a series of six consecutive stronger yuan mid point fixings.\par \par \uc2  The 1-month dollar/yuan NDF slid to as low as 6.5030 and the 1-year NDF fell to 6.3605, the lowest since April 2008. That implied spot yuan appreciation of 2.4 percent in the next year, slightly more than the 2.2 percent implied by the one-year NDF a week ago.\par \par \uc2  Earlier, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will open domestic bond market further to overseas investors. [ID:nB9E7EN01L]\par \par \uc2  "PBOC said that they will accelerate opening of its bond market, though acknowledging inflows will add to CNY appreciation. So maybe investors are now betting on a faster CNY appreciation," said Frances Cheung, a strategist at Credit Agricole CIB in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2  RINGGIT\par \par \uc2  Demand from interbank speculators and leveraged names lift the ringgit  to a two-week high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2  The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to as firm as 3.0200 per dollar, the strongest since March 25.\par \par \uc2  Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying dollars, but it also followed its Asian peers lowering levels of dollar bids.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been guarding 3.0250 versus the greenback, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 3.0220, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  RUPEE\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  rupee  hit a five-month high against the dollar on demand from interbank speculators and leveraged accounts.\par \par \uc2  The rupee strengthened to as firm as 43.98, the strongest since Oct 15, 2010. If it clearly breaks through 43.97, the high of Oct 15 last year, demand for the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen increasing more.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet, that could attract fast money and funds for catch-up buying.\par \par \uc2  The rupee returned to levels of 44 per dollar, but that was mainly because of dollar demand from oil importers.\par \par \uc2  The rupee has risen 1.5 percent against the dollar so far this year, the second worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Thai baht among emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR                                  \par \par \uc2  Change on the day at 0700 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        85.05          84.91       -0.16\par  Sing dlr        1.2569         1.2601       +0.25\par  Taiwan dlr      28.914         29.050       +0.47\par  Korean won     1082.4