\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee held in tight band; dlr rise weighs\b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2010\par 05:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Dollar gains versus majors, other Asians; weighs on rupee\par \par \uc2 * Share gains help hold rupee in tight range, limit downside\par \par \uc2 * INR seen rising to 43/dlr levels by March 2011 - Yes Bank (Updates to mid-morning)\par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 9 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was held in a tight range on Tuesday as gains in domestic shares were offset by broad gains in the dollar versus other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and major units.\par \par \uc2 At 10:25 a.m. (0455 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 44.38/39 per dollar, unchanged from the close on Monday. The unit has so far traded in the range of 44.3575 to 44.42.\par \par \uc2 "There is some risk aversion in the market broadly because of the euro zone debt issue but how much that affects the foreign fund inflows to India, one cannot be sure. Shares are higher today," a senior dealer with a private bank said.\par \par \uc2 Local shares <.BSESN> were trading up 0.4 percent due to foreign fund inflows after having opened marginally lower. [.BO]\par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have so far in 2010 bought shares worth a record $28.1 billion, in addition to last year's $17.5 billion. The rupee has gained 4.8 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 "A very rangebound session so far, it should remain like this. 44.30-44.50 seems like a good stable range. Even though local shares are positive, euro downside is halting rupee gains," a senior dealer with a state-run bank said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's <.DXY> index against six majors was 0.2 percent higher and was being watched for cues.\par \par \uc2 The euro's losses deepened on Tuesday as resurfacing concerns about peripheral euro zone debt kept it under pressure, and as short-term players closed dollar short positions as they prepared for year-end book-closing. [USD/]\par \par \uc2 Traders said they were also watching for inflows towards \uc2 Power Grid Corp of India\uc2 's follow-on public offer. The world's third-largest power transmission company on Tuesday launches a share sale to raise up to $1.7 billion before it closes on Friday. [ID:nSGE6A707O]\par \par \uc2 "The small amount of real appreciation (in the rupee) is unlikely to have a significant implication for competitiveness," economists at Yes Bank said in a recent note, citing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy statement which said the rupee has risen by only 0.4 percent on a broad real effective exchange rate basis.\par \par \uc2 "This gives us comfort in expecting the RBI (\uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to stay away from any significant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the back of an increase in the absorptive capacity of the economy and also because of latent inflationary threats," the note said.\par \par \uc2 "Hence we continue to expect (the) rupee to appreciate on a trend basis to 43.00 levels by March 2011."\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore non-deliverable forward contracts <PNDF> were at 44.63, weaker than the onshore spot rate.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market <INRFUTURES>, the most traded near-month dollar-rupee contracts on the National Stock Exchange, MCX-SX and United Stock Exchange were all at 44.55, with the total traded volume on the three exchanges at about $1.1 billion. (Reporting by Swati Bhat; Editing by Bryson Hull)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|SNS|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101112e6b9000ae\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000